    "tagline": "Attention, tokens, sampling, context, hallucination, evals and inference cost: the LLM questions AI-engineer interviews really ask.",
    "description": "A 450-question, provider-agnostic bank on how large language models work and how to use them well, served as 40-question, 60-minute mocks: transformer architecture and attention, tokenization and embeddings, pretraining versus fine-tuning and alignment (SFT, RLHF, DPO, LoRA/QLoRA), decoding and sampling parameters, context windows and prompting, hallucination and grounding, evaluation and LLM-as-judge, choosing between prompting, RAG and fine-tuning, inference economics and serving, and safety basics such as jailbreaks and prompt injection. Written against the field as of October 2026: Hugging Face Transformers 5.20, PEFT 0.21, TRL 1.16, vLLM 0.32 and the OWASP Top 10 for LLM Applications (2025). Every option explains its reasoning.",
